sentences.l:
But come, cut the tongues, and mix the wine,
so that to Poseidon and the other immortals
having poured libations, of bed we may take thought;

And for them the heralds poured water over their hands,
and young men filled the mixing-bowls to the brim with drink,
and they dealt it out to all, having first poured drops into the cups;

and for them, when they had come, the old man mixed a bowl
of sweet-to-drink wine, which in its eleventh year
the housekeeper opened, and loosed off its covering;
